\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The lack of a date notice makes the first oracle of Ezekiel 30 difficult to place in its original context. But its placement after Ezekiel 29 lets us pay close attention to Ezekiel 29 and its message to understand how to read 30.\
And what I see first is the raw power of 'I am against you' in 29, and the day of the LORD in 30.\
But you might see something different, trying to understand in your own way the rhetoric of this first oracle of Ezekiel 30.
